{"Negative offset handling in OptimizedCursorPaginator may yield incorrect pages because Python list slicing interprets negative indices as counting from end of result list when is_prev is True": 0.6169847249984741, "Cursor class allows negative offsets without strong validation, creating potential edge-case bugs in paging logic": 0.180116668343544, "Advanced pagination path in audit logs endpoint introduces conditional behavior depending on request params and user roles; misconfiguration or edge cases could affect paging correctness or performance for high-volume audit logs": 0.19319985806941986, "Typo in build_queryset: code writes to queryset.order_b (missing trailing 'y') instead of queryset.query.order_by, causing AttributeError or silently failing to change ordering, breaking pagination": 0.0183145422488451, "Duplicate OptimizedCursorPaginator class definitions in paginator.py where second definition overwrites first, leaving class without required get_result method and causing runtime failures": 0.025337833911180496, "Redis span buffer changes from sets to sorted sets (zset) alters data structure semantics; consumers relying on set semantics or member ordering could break": 0.7506950497627258, "Span NamedTuple now requires end_timestamp_precise field, breaking any code paths that construct Span without this field": 0.8726138472557068, "Redis buffering switches from sadd/sunionstore to zadd/zunionstore; any consumer assuming set-based storage may break": 0.745293915271759, "Segment data loading changed to zscan instead of sscan; if zscan_values format differs this could lead to missed spans or incorrect sizing": 0.5496594905853271, "Span ingestion unconditionally accesses val['end_timestamp_precise'] which will raise KeyError if producer omits this field, causing ingestion failures": 0.9319510459899902, "Test fixtures include end_timestamp_precise but if production data diverges, real-world ingestion could be affected": 0.36507371068000793, "Misleading comment